IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-groups`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026
-- (a rendering, not the official text). Part 5 Division 2, s 156: a director's or chief executive officer's duty to disclose an interest in a transaction,
-- or a conflicting office or property, and the offence of not doing so.
-- Whether a corporation is related to the company by s 6 is the keel's answer (sg-groups.l4), taken as one fact.
-- JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say.
-- "As soon as practicable" is not a number, so no function here can say a declaration is late (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).

§ `Section 156: disclosure of interests in transactions, property, offices and so on`

DECLARE `s 156(15) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (13): an interest of a member of the director's (or chief executive officer's) family is treated as an interest of the director; the words include a spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and stepdaughter.
DECLARE `s 156(13) relationship to the director or chief executive officer` IS ONE OF
    `s 156(13) spouse`
    `s 156(13) son`
    `s 156(13) adopted son`
    `s 156(13) stepson`
    `s 156(13) daughter`
    `s 156(13) adopted daughter`
    `s 156(13) stepdaughter`
    `s 156(13) another relation`

-- src:13137 | (13) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:13139 | (a) an interest of a member of a director’s family is treated as
-- src:13140 | an interest of the director and the words “member of a
-- src:13141 | director’s family” include his or her spouse, son, adopted
-- src:13142 | son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and stepdaughter;
-- src:13143 | and
-- src:13145 | (b) an interest of a member of a chief executive officer’s
-- src:13146 | family is treated as an interest of the chief executive officer
-- src:13147 | and the words “member of the chief executive officer’s
-- src:13148 | family” include his or her spouse, son, adopted son,
-- src:13149 | stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and stepdaughter.
@ref s 156(13) (src:13137-13149)
GIVEN `the relationship of the person who has the interest` IS A `s 156(13) relationship to the director or chief executive officer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(13) the person is a member of the director's or chief executive officer's family whose interest is treated as an interest of the director or chief executive officer` MEANS
    IF `the relationship of the person who has the interest` EQUALS `s 156(13) another relation`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the words “member of a director’s family” include his or her spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter and stepdaughter" leaves the list open
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3): the requirements of (1) do not apply where the interest consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation which is interested in the transaction,
-- if the interest may properly be regarded as not being a material interest.
-- src:12969 | (3) The requirements of subsection (1) do not apply in any case
-- src:12970 | where the interest of the director or chief executive officer (as the
-- src:12971 | case may be) consists only of being a member or creditor of a
-- src:12972 | corporation which is interested in a transaction or proposed
-- src:12973 | transaction with the firstmentioned company if the interest of the
-- src:12978 | director or chief executive officer (as the case may be) may properly
-- src:12979 | be regarded as not being a material interest.
@ref s 156(3) (src:12969-12979)
GIVEN `the interest of the director or chief executive officer consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation which is interested in the transaction or proposed transaction with the firstmentioned company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest may properly be regarded as not being a material interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(3) the requirements of subsection (1) do not apply` MEANS
    IF `the interest of the director or chief executive officer consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation which is interested in the transaction or proposed transaction with the firstmentioned company` AND `the interest may properly be regarded as not being a material interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements of subsection (1) do not apply in any case where the interest ... consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation ... if the interest ... may properly be regarded as not being a material interest" -- a "where" gate (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)) that fails

-- (4): not deemed to be interested by reason only of (a) having guaranteed a loan to the company, or (b) being a director or chief executive officer of a corporation deemed related to the company by s 6.
-- src:12983 | (4) A director or chief executive officer of a company is not deemed
-- src:12984 | to be interested or to have been at any time interested in any
-- src:12985 | transaction or proposed transaction by reason only —
-- src:12987 | (a) in the case where the transaction or proposed transaction
-- src:12988 | relates to any loan to the company — that he or she has
-- src:12989 | guaranteed or joined in guaranteeing the repayment of the
-- src:12990 | loan or any part of the loan; or
-- src:12992 | (b) in the case where the transaction or proposed transaction
-- src:12993 | has been or will be made with or for the benefit of or on
-- src:12994 | behalf of a corporation which by virtue of section 6 is
-- src:12995 | deemed to be related to the company — that he or she is a
-- src:12996 | director or chief executive officer (as the case may be) of
-- src:12997 | that corporation,
@ref s 156(4) (src:12983-12997)
GIVEN `the transaction or proposed transaction relates to a loan to the company and the director or chief executive officer has guaranteed or joined in guaranteeing the repayment of the loan or any part of the loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction or proposed transaction has been or will be made with or for the benefit of or on behalf of a corporation which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director or chief executive officer is a director or chief executive officer of that corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is the only reason the director or chief executive officer would be treated as interested in the transaction or proposed transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(4) the director or chief executive officer is not deemed to be interested in the transaction by reason only of the guarantee or the office` MEANS
    IF    `that is the only reason the director or chief executive officer would be treated as interested in the transaction or proposed transaction`
      AND (   `the transaction or proposed transaction relates to a loan to the company and the director or chief executive officer has guaranteed or joined in guaranteeing the repayment of the loan or any part of the loan`
           OR (   `s 4(1) "related corporation" the other corporation is a related corporation of the corporation` `the transaction or proposed transaction has been or will be made with or for the benefit of or on behalf of a corporation which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `the director or chief executive officer is a director or chief executive officer of that corporation`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is not deemed to be interested ... by reason only -- (a) ...; or (b) ..." names two reasons and says nothing of others

DECLARE `s 156(4) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 156(4) the purposes of this Act`
    `s 156(4) the purposes of any other law`
    `s 156(4) a provision in the constitution of the company`

-- src:12999 | and this subsection has effect not only for the purposes of this Act but
-- src:13000 | also for the purposes of any other law, but does not affect the
-- src:13001 | operation of any provision in the constitution of the company.
@ref s 156(4) (src:12999-13001)
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 156(4) purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(4) the subsection has effect for the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `s 156(4) the purposes of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 156(4) the purposes of any other law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 156(4) a provision in the constitution of the company` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this subsection has effect not only for the purposes of this Act but also for the purposes of any other law, but does not affect the operation of any provision in the constitution of the company"

-- (1): every director or chief executive officer of a company who is in any way, directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company must,
-- as soon as practicable after the relevant facts come to his or her knowledge, (a) declare the nature of the interest at a meeting of the directors, or (b) send a written notice.
-- src:12938 | 156.—(1) Subject to this section, every director or chief executive
-- src:12939 | officer of a company who is in any way, whether directly or indirectly,
-- src:12940 | interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company
-- src:12941 | must as soon as is practicable after the relevant facts have come to his
-- src:12942 | or her knowledge —
-- src:12944 | (a) declare the nature of his or her interest at a meeting of the
-- src:12945 | directors of the company; or
-- src:12947 | (b) send a written notice to the company containing details on
-- src:12948 | the nature, character and extent of his or her interest in the
-- src:12949 | transaction or proposed transaction with the company.
@ref s 156(1) (src:12938-12949)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in any way, whether directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not deemed to be interested by reason of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest of the director or chief executive officer consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation which is interested in the transaction or proposed transaction with the firstmentioned company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest may properly be regarded as not being a material interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the nature of the interest or send a written notice` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` AND `the person is in any way, whether directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every director or chief executive officer of a company who is in any way, whether directly or indirectly, interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF `the person is not deemed to be interested by reason of subsection (4)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A director or chief executive officer of a company is not deemed to be interested or to have been at any time interested in any transaction or proposed transaction by reason only" (subsection (4))
          ELSE (IF `s 156(3) the requirements of subsection (1) do not apply` `the interest of the director or chief executive officer consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation which is interested in the transaction or proposed transaction with the firstmentioned company` `the interest may properly be regarded as not being a material interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements of subsection (1) do not apply in any case where the interest ... consists only of being a member or creditor of a corporation" (subsection (3))
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

@ref s 156(1) (src:12944-12949)
GIVEN `the person declares the nature of his or her interest at a meeting of the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person sends a written notice to the company containing details on the nature, character and extent of his or her interest in the transaction or proposed transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(1) the person has made the declaration or sent the written notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the person declares the nature of his or her interest at a meeting of the directors of the company` OR `the person sends a written notice to the company containing details on the nature, character and extent of his or her interest in the transaction or proposed transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must as soon as is practicable ... (a) declare the nature of his or her interest at a meeting of the directors of the company; or (b) send a written notice to the company" (a duty not met, the provision's own question)

-- (2) and (8): the date from which the notice must be given as soon as practicable: the day the person became a director or chief executive officer, or, if already one, the day the person became interested
-- (subsection (2)(b)) or commenced to hold the office or possess the property (subsection (8)(b)).
-- src:12953 | (2) A notice under subsection (1)(b) must be given as soon as is
-- src:12954 | practicable after —
-- src:12956 | (a) the date on which the director or chief executive officer
-- src:12957 | became a director or chief executive officer (as the case
-- src:12958 | may be); or
-- src:12960 | (b) (if already a director or chief executive officer, as the case
-- src:12961 | may be) the date on which the director or chief executive
-- src:12962 | officer became, directly or indirectly, interested in a
-- src:12963 | transaction or proposed transaction with the company,
-- src:12965 | as the case requires.
@ref s 156(2) (src:12953-12965)
GIVEN `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she became interested in the transaction or proposed transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the person became a director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the person became, directly or indirectly, interested in the transaction or proposed transaction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 156(2) the date after which the notice under subsection (1)(b) must be given as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she became interested in the transaction or proposed transaction`
    THEN `the date on which the person became, directly or indirectly, interested in the transaction or proposed transaction`
    ELSE `the date on which the person became a director or chief executive officer`

-- src:13074 | (8) A written notice under subsection (6)(b) must be given as soon
-- src:13075 | as is practicable after —
-- src:13080 | (a) the date on which the director or chief executive officer
-- src:13081 | became a director or chief executive officer (as the case
-- src:13082 | may be); or
-- src:13084 | (b) (if already a director or chief executive officer, as the case
-- src:13085 | may be) after he or she commenced to hold the office or to
-- src:13086 | possess the property,
-- src:13088 | as the case requires.
@ref s 156(8) (src:13074-13088)
GIVEN `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the person became a director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the person commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 156(8) the date after which the written notice under subsection (6)(b) must be given as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she commenced to hold the office or to possess the property`
    THEN `the date on which the person commenced to hold the office or to possess the property`
    ELSE `the date on which the person became a director or chief executive officer`

-- (5): a general declaration or notice about a specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership is a sufficient declaration or notice for later transactions if (a) to (d) hold.
DECLARE `s 156(5) kind of paper` IS ONE OF
    `s 156(5) a declaration under subsection (1)(a)`
    `s 156(5) a written notice under subsection (1)(b)`

-- src:13005 | (5) A declaration given by a director or chief executive officer
-- src:13006 | under subsection (1)(a), or a written notice given by a director or
-- src:13007 | chief executive officer under subsection (1)(b), is to be treated as a
-- src:13008 | sufficient declaration or written notice under those provisions in
-- src:13009 | relation to a transaction or proposed transaction if —
-- src:13011 | (a) in the case of a declaration, the declaration is given at a
-- src:13012 | meeting of the directors or the director or chief executive
-- src:13013 | officer (as the case may be) takes reasonable steps to
-- src:13014 | ensure that it is brought up and read at the next meeting of
-- src:13015 | the directors after it is given;
-- src:13017 | (b) the declaration or written notice is to the effect that —
-- src:13019 | (i) he or she is an officer or a member of a specified
-- src:13020 | corporation, a member of a specified firm, or a
-- src:13021 | partner or officer of a specified limited liability
-- src:13022 | partnership; and
-- src:13027 | (ii) he or she is to be regarded as interested in any
-- src:13028 | transaction which may, after the date of the
-- src:13029 | declaration or written notice, be made with the
-- src:13030 | specified corporation, firm or limited liability
-- src:13031 | partnership;
-- src:13033 | (c) the declaration or written notice specifies the nature and
-- src:13034 | extent of his or her interest in the specified corporation,
-- src:13035 | firm or limited liability partnership; and
-- src:13037 | (d) at the time the transaction is made, or the proposed
-- src:13038 | transaction is proposed, his or her interest is not different in
-- src:13039 | nature or greater in extent than the nature and extent
-- src:13040 | specified in the declaration or written notice.
@ref s 156(5) (src:13005-13040)
GIVEN `the kind of paper` IS A `s 156(5) kind of paper`
      `the declaration is given at a meeting of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes reasonable steps to ensure that the declaration is brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is an officer or a member of a specified corporation, a member of a specified firm, or a partner or officer of a specified limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is to be regarded as interested in any transaction which may, after its date, be made with the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration or written notice specifies the nature and extent of the person's interest in the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the transaction is made, or the proposed transaction is proposed, the person's interest is not different in nature or greater in extent than the nature and extent specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(5) the declaration or written notice is treated as a sufficient declaration or written notice in relation to the transaction` MEANS
    IF    (CONSIDER `the kind of paper`
           WHEN `s 156(5) a declaration under subsection (1)(a)` THEN (`the declaration is given at a meeting of the directors` OR `the person takes reasonable steps to ensure that the declaration is brought up and read at the next meeting of the directors after it is given`)
           WHEN `s 156(5) a written notice under subsection (1)(b)` THEN TRUE)
      AND `the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is an officer or a member of a specified corporation, a member of a specified firm, or a partner or officer of a specified limited liability partnership`
      AND `the declaration or written notice is to the effect that the person is to be regarded as interested in any transaction which may, after its date, be made with the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership`
      AND `the declaration or written notice specifies the nature and extent of the person's interest in the specified corporation, firm or limited liability partnership`
      AND `at the time the transaction is made, or the proposed transaction is proposed, the person's interest is not different in nature or greater in extent than the nature and extent specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be treated as a sufficient declaration or written notice ... if -- (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." -- a condition introduced with "if" that fails (marginal reading (a), fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (6): every director and chief executive officer who holds any office or possesses any property whereby a duty or interest might be created in conflict must declare it at a meeting of the directors or send a written notice.
-- src:13046 | (6) Every director and chief executive officer of a company who
-- src:13047 | holds any office or possess any property whereby, whether directly or
-- src:13048 | indirectly, any duty or interest might be created in conflict with their
-- src:13049 | duties or interests as director or chief executive officer (as the case
-- src:13050 | may be) must —
-- src:13052 | (a) declare at a meeting of the directors of the company the
-- src:13053 | fact and the nature, character and extent of the conflict; or
-- src:13055 | (b) send a written notice to the company setting out the fact
-- src:13056 | and the nature, character and extent of the conflict.
@ref s 156(6) (src:13046-13056)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds any office or possesses any property whereby, whether directly or indirectly, any duty or interest might be created in conflict with the person's duties or interests as director or chief executive officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict or send a written notice` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` AND `the person holds any office or possesses any property whereby, whether directly or indirectly, any duty or interest might be created in conflict with the person's duties or interests as director or chief executive officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every director and chief executive officer of a company who holds any office or possess any property whereby ... any duty or interest might be created in conflict" -- a scope limit with no "only"

@ref s 156(6) (src:13052-13056)
GIVEN `the person declares at a meeting of the directors of the company the fact and the nature, character and extent of the conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person sends a written notice to the company setting out the fact and the nature, character and extent of the conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(6) the person has made the declaration or sent the written notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the person declares at a meeting of the directors of the company the fact and the nature, character and extent of the conflict` OR `the person sends a written notice to the company setting out the fact and the nature, character and extent of the conflict`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must -- (a) declare at a meeting of the directors of the company the fact and the nature, character and extent of the conflict; or (b) send a written notice" (a duty not met, the provision's own question)

-- (7): a declaration under (6)(a) must be made at the first meeting of the directors held after the person becomes a director or chief executive officer, or, if already one, after the person commenced to hold the office or possess the property.
GIVEN `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer, or commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` IS A DATE
      `the dates of the meetings of the directors` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 156(7) the first of the meetings held after the date` MEANS
    foldr (GIVEN d, acc YIELD
            IF d GREATER THAN `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer, or commenced to hold the office or to possess the property`
            THEN (CONSIDER acc
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST d
                  WHEN JUST e THEN JUST (IF d LESS THAN e THEN d ELSE e))
            ELSE acc)
          NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the starting value of the fold; it is the answer only when no meeting of the directors is held after the date, and the text says nothing of that case
          `the dates of the meetings of the directors`

-- src:13060 | (7) A declaration under subsection (6)(a) must be made at the first
-- src:13061 | meeting of the directors of the company held —
-- src:13063 | (a) after he or she becomes a director or chief executive officer
-- src:13064 | (as the case may be); or
-- src:13066 | (b) (if already a director or chief executive officer, as the case
-- src:13067 | may be) after he or she commenced to hold the office or to
-- src:13068 | possess the property,
-- src:13070 | as the case requires.
@ref s 156(7) (src:13060-13070)
GIVEN `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE
      `the date the person commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` IS A DATE
      `the dates of the meetings of the directors` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 156(7) the meeting of the directors at which the declaration under subsection (6)(a) must be made` MEANS
    IF `the person was already a director or chief executive officer when he or she commenced to hold the office or to possess the property`
    THEN `s 156(7) the first of the meetings held after the date` `the date the person commenced to hold the office or to possess the property` `the dates of the meetings of the directors`
    ELSE `s 156(7) the first of the meetings held after the date` `the date the person became a director or chief executive officer` `the dates of the meetings of the directors`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): where no meeting of the directors has been held after that date, the answer is NOTHING: the subsection names the first meeting held after and none has been held

-- (9): the company must send a copy of the written notice to all the directors (a notice given by a chief executive officer) or all the other directors (a notice given by a director).
DECLARE `s 156(9) to whom the company must send a copy` IS ONE OF
    `s 156(9)(a) all the directors`
    `s 156(9)(b) all the other directors`
    `s 156(9) no one the subsection names`

-- src:13092 | (9) The company must, as soon as practicable after the receipt of the
-- src:13093 | written notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b), send a copy of
-- src:13094 | the notice to —
-- src:13096 | (a) in the case where the notice is given by a chief executive
-- src:13097 | officer — all the directors; or
-- src:13099 | (b) in the case where the notice is given by a director — all the
-- src:13100 | other directors.
@ref s 156(9) (src:13092-13100)
GIVEN `the company has received the written notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given by a chief executive officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given by a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 156(9) to whom the company must send a copy`
`s 156(9) the persons to whom the company must send a copy of the notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has received the written notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b)`
    THEN `s 156(9) no one the subsection names`
    ELSE (IF `the notice is given by a chief executive officer`
          THEN `s 156(9)(a) all the directors`
          ELSE (IF `the notice is given by a director`
                THEN `s 156(9)(b) all the other directors`
                ELSE `s 156(9) no one the subsection names`))

-- (10): where a director or chief executive officer declares an interest or conflict by written notice in accordance with the section, the declaration is deemed to form part of the proceedings at the next meeting of the directors
-- after the notice is given, and s 188 (minutes of proceedings) applies as if the declaration had been made at that meeting.
-- src:13104 | (10) Where a chief executive officer or a director of the company
-- src:13105 | declares an interest or conflict by a written notice mentioned in
-- src:13106 | subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b) (respectively) in accordance with this
-- src:13107 | section —
-- src:13109 | (a) the making of the declaration is deemed to form part of the
-- src:13110 | proceedings at the next meeting of the directors after the
-- src:13111 | notice is given; and
@ref s 156(10)(a) (src:13104-13111)
GIVEN `the director or chief executive officer declares an interest or conflict by a written notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b) in accordance with section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(10)(a) the declaration is deemed to form part of the proceedings at the next meeting of the directors after the notice is given` MEANS
    IF `the director or chief executive officer declares an interest or conflict by a written notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b) in accordance with section 156`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a chief executive officer or a director of the company declares an interest or conflict by a written notice ... in accordance with this section -- (a) the making of the declaration is deemed to form part of the proceedings" -- a "where" gate (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)) that fails

-- src:13104 | (10) Where a chief executive officer or a director of the company
-- src:13105 | declares an interest or conflict by a written notice mentioned in
-- src:13106 | subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b) (respectively) in accordance with this
-- src:13107 | section —
-- src:13109 | (a) the making of the declaration is deemed to form part of the
-- src:13110 | proceedings at the next meeting of the directors after the
-- src:13111 | notice is given; and
-- src:13113 | (b) the provisions of section 188 (minutes of proceedings)
-- src:13114 | apply as if the declaration had been made at that meeting.
@ref s 156(10)(b) (src:13104-13114)
GIVEN `the director or chief executive officer declares an interest or conflict by a written notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b) in accordance with section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(10)(b) section 188 applies as if the declaration had been made at that meeting` MEANS
    IF `the director or chief executive officer declares an interest or conflict by a written notice mentioned in subsection (1)(b) or (6)(b) in accordance with section 156`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... (b) the provisions of section 188 (minutes of proceedings) apply as if the declaration had been made at that meeting" -- a "where" gate that fails

-- (11): the secretary must record every declaration made at a meeting in the minutes and keep records of every written resolution duly signed and returned.
-- src:13118 | (11) The secretary of the company must record every declaration
-- src:13119 | under this section in the minutes of the meeting at which it was made
-- src:13120 | and keep records of every written resolution duly signed and returned
-- src:13121 | to the company under this section.
@ref s 156(11) (src:13118-13121)
GIVEN `a declaration under section 156 was made at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(11) the secretary must record the declaration in the minutes of the meeting at which it was made` MEANS
    IF `a declaration under section 156 was made at a meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must record every declaration under this section in the minutes of the meeting at which it was made" -- a scope limit with no "only"

@ref s 156(11) (src:13119-13121)
GIVEN `a written resolution is duly signed and returned to the company under section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(11) the secretary must keep a record of the written resolution` MEANS
    IF `a written resolution is duly signed and returned to the company under section 156`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "keep records of every written resolution duly signed and returned to the company under this section" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- (12): the directors must permit a chief executive officer who is not a director to attend a board meeting where attendance is necessary to make a declaration.
-- src:13125 | (12) The directors of a company must permit a chief executive
-- src:13126 | officer of the company who is not a director to attend a meeting of the
-- src:13127 | board of directors where such attendance is necessary for the chief
-- src:13132 | executive officer to make a declaration for the purpose of complying
-- src:13133 | with this section.
@ref s 156(12) (src:13125-13133)
GIVEN `the person is a chief executive officer of the company who is not a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `attendance is necessary for the chief executive officer to make a declaration for the purpose of complying with section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(12) the directors must permit the chief executive officer to attend the meeting of the board of directors` MEANS
    IF `the person is a chief executive officer of the company who is not a director` AND `attendance is necessary for the chief executive officer to make a declaration for the purpose of complying with section 156`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must permit a chief executive officer of the company who is not a director to attend a meeting of the board of directors where such attendance is necessary" -- a "where" gate (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)) that fails

-- (14): subject to (4), the section is in addition to and not in derogation of any rule of law or provision in the constitution restricting a director or chief executive officer from having an interest in transactions with the company or from holding conflicting offices or properties.
-- src:13153 | (14) Subject to subsection (4), this section is in addition to and not
-- src:13154 | in derogation of the operation of any rule of law or any provision in
-- src:13155 | the constitution restricting a director or chief executive officer from
-- src:13156 | having any interest in transactions with the company or from holding
-- src:13157 | offices or possessing properties involving duties or interests in
-- src:13158 | conflict with his or her duties or interests as a director or chief
-- src:13159 | executive officer (as the case may be).
@ref s 156(14) (src:13153-13159)
GIVEN `a rule of law or a provision in the constitution restricts a director or chief executive officer from having an interest in transactions with the company or from holding offices or possessing properties involving duties or interests in conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is one to which subsection (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(14) the section derogates from the rule of law or the provision in the constitution` MEANS
    IF `the matter is one to which subsection (4) applies`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (4)" -- where subsection (4) applies the text says no more here
    ELSE (IF `a rule of law or a provision in the constitution restricts a director or chief executive officer from having an interest in transactions with the company or from holding offices or possessing properties involving duties or interests in conflict`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section is in addition to and not in derogation of the operation of any rule of law or any provision in the constitution restricting a director or chief executive officer from having any interest in transactions with the company"
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of rules and provisions that restrict such interests and offices

-- (15): any director or chief executive officer who fails to comply with any of the provisions of the section is guilty of an offence.
-- src:13163 | (15) Any director or chief executive officer of a company who fails
-- src:13164 | to comply with any of the provisions of this section shall be guilty of
-- src:13165 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:13166 | $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 156(15) (src:13163-13166)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with any of the provisions of section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 156(15) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` AND `the person fails to comply with any of the provisions of section 156`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Any director or chief executive officer of a company who fails to comply with any of the provisions of this section shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 156(15) (src:13163-13166)
GIVEN `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with any of the provisions of section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 156(15) penalty`
`s 156(15) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 156(15) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is a director or chief executive officer of the company` `the person fails to comply with any of the provisions of section 156` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 156(15) penalty` OF 5000, 12, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months: the text says "or", not "or to both" (fork line in NOTES.md)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Regulative rules: section 156(1), (6) and (7), (11) and (12)`

DECLARE `s 156 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 156(1) declare the nature of the interest at a meeting of the directors, or send a written notice to the company`
    `s 156(6) declare the conflict at a meeting of the directors, or send a written notice to the company`
    `s 156(7) declare the conflict at the first meeting of the directors held after the date`
    `s 156(11) record the declaration in the minutes`
    `s 156(12) permit the chief executive officer to attend the meeting of the board of directors`

-- (1): "as soon as is practicable" is not a number of days: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH.
-- src:12938 | 156.—(1) Subject to this section, every director or chief executive
-- src:12939 | officer of a company who is in any way, whether directly or indirectly,
-- src:12940 | interested in a transaction or proposed transaction with the company
-- src:12941 | must as soon as is practicable after the relevant facts have come to his
-- src:12942 | or her knowledge —
-- src:12944 | (a) declare the nature of his or her interest at a meeting of the
-- src:12945 | directors of the company; or
-- src:12947 | (b) send a written notice to the company containing details on
-- src:12948 | the nature, character and extent of his or her interest in the
-- src:12949 | transaction or proposed transaction with the company.
@ref s 156(1) (src:12938-12949)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 156 act`
`s 156(1) a director must declare the nature of the interest` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 156(1) declare the nature of the interest at a meeting of the directors, or send a written notice to the company`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- the section says "as soon as is practicable"; read as Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not declare the nature of the interest or send a written notice"

-- (6) and (7): the declaration of a conflict must be made at the first meeting held after; the clock counts days from the trigger to that meeting.
-- src:13060 | (7) A declaration under subsection (6)(a) must be made at the first
-- src:13061 | meeting of the directors of the company held —
-- src:13063 | (a) after he or she becomes a director or chief executive officer
-- src:13064 | (as the case may be); or
-- src:13066 | (b) (if already a director or chief executive officer, as the case
-- src:13067 | may be) after he or she commenced to hold the office or to
-- src:13068 | possess the property,
-- src:13070 | as the case requires.
@ref s 156(7) (src:13060-13070)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the date the person became a director or chief executive officer, or commenced to hold the office or to possess the property, to the first meeting of the directors held after it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 156 act`
`s 156(7) a director must declare the conflict at the first meeting of the directors held after` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 156(7) declare the conflict at the first meeting of the directors held after the date`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the date the person became a director or chief executive officer, or commenced to hold the office or to possess the property, to the first meeting of the directors held after it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not declare the conflict at the first meeting of the directors held after becoming a director or after commencing to hold the office or possess the property"

-- src:13118 | (11) The secretary of the company must record every declaration
-- src:13119 | under this section in the minutes of the meeting at which it was made
-- src:13120 | and keep records of every written resolution duly signed and returned
-- src:13121 | to the company under this section.
@ref s 156(11) (src:13118-13121)
GIVEN `the name of the secretary` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 156 act`
`s 156(11) the secretary must record every declaration in the minutes` MEANS
    PARTY Secretary `the name of the secretary`
    MUST `s 156(11) record the declaration in the minutes`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 156(11) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Secretary `the name of the secretary` BECAUSE "the secretary did not record the declaration in the minutes of the meeting at which it was made" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- src:13125 | (12) The directors of a company must permit a chief executive
-- src:13126 | officer of the company who is not a director to attend a meeting of the
-- src:13127 | board of directors where such attendance is necessary for the chief
-- src:13132 | executive officer to make a declaration for the purpose of complying
-- src:13133 | with this section.
@ref s 156(12) (src:13125-13133)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 156 act`
`s 156(12) the directors must permit the chief executive officer to attend` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 156(12) permit the chief executive officer to attend the meeting of the board of directors`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 156(12) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not permit a chief executive officer who is not a director to attend a meeting of the board where attendance was necessary to make a declaration" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]
